@0pdd let me amend the requirement in this puzzle: none of the example decorators should close the inputstream. We could have an `HtAutoClosedResponse` though. Consider that in #63 we basically want to keep the socket alive unless we explicitly close it.

Example:

```java
new HtAutoClosedResponse(            //automatically closes stream/socket when EOF is reached  
    new HtContentLengthResponse(     //reads inputstream up to length received in Content-Length
        new HtResponse(              //inputstream as-is
            new HtWire("host"),
            "request"
        )
    )
)
```

